            <div xml:id="d592">

                <pb facs="0562" n="554" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg554"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.61331/239: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-11-30T19:00:00+09:00">November 30, 1940—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 1—4:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1245. Our 1212, November 27, noon,<anchor n="43" xml:id="d592-f1"/> Universal
                    Leaf Tobacco Company. In conversation with the Foreign Minister today, I
                    repeated our representations of November 27 in an effort to impress the Minister
                    with the particularly flagrant character of this case of interference with the
                    legitimate and long established rights of this company. Mr. Matsuoka made notes
                    of my remarks and said that he would pursue the matter.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department via Peiping. Peiping please repeat to Chungking, Tientsin
                    and Tsingtao.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
